1
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:10,900
His fast-acting mind is one reason.

2
00:00:17,240 --> 00:00:18,160
Wake up!

3
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:22,439
If you start napping now, it's gonna
be hard to get to sleep tonight.

4
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:27,237
There's three days of winter break left
and your homework won't finish itself.

5
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:29,917
Sinon finished hers before
heading back home to visit.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,717
Just saying I'm so sleepy poor thing it's
probably because the room's too warm.

7
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,777
You want me to turn down the heat?

8
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:44,797
It's not the heat it's the masters
of the sleep skill over there huh?

9
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,940
Oh well that figures.

10
00:00:56,020 --> 00:00:59,777
He's been working hard on his project
ever since he got back from GGO.

11
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,897
You mean that gizmo for Yui he
demoed the other day at Egil's?

12
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,215
Oh, the mechaphonics?

13
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,220
No, it's called mechatronics.

14
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:07,840
Uh, yeah, that.

15
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:10,717
Anyway, he's napping
like there's no tomorrow.

16
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:11,630
Look at him.

17
00:01:11,713 --> 00:01:13,028
He's making me feel sleepy.

18
00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:19,770
Hmm.

19
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:52,697
I see nothing in the way it is.

20
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:57,217
I don't know what it is.

21
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:00,077
I hear the voice in the voice.

22
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,797
I'm not sure what it is.

23
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:04,497
I hear the message

24
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:08,940
from the beginning.

25
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:14,840
I hear the word that
I'm going to turn into.

26
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,160
Here you go.

27
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,800
Yo, guys, seriously.

28
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:12,077
Y 'all don't have to come here
every time you're on a date.

29
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,757
There's classier places
in town you could go to.

30
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,017
What are you talking about?

31
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:19,977
This place is plenty classy, compared
to your shop in Allgate anyway.

32
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:22,560
Oh, don't listen to him. I liked it.

33
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,251
That place was a rip-off.

34
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,137
Half that junk was paper mache.

35
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,477
How can you say that?

36
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,277
He was letting you stay there for free.

37
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,897
That's got nothing to do with it.

38
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:31,810
Oh, whatever.

39
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:35,022
Okay, Spill It, what's so funny?

40
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:36,990
Nothing.

41
00:03:37,073 --> 00:03:38,440
Just, seeing you like this,

42
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:41,877
y 'all don't look anything like
the Assault Team's top players.

43
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,431
Right back at you, buddy.

44
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:48,660
Well, on that note, I bet you've
played MMORPGs for a long time, huh?

45
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,470
True that.

46
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:52,357
I played so much, I met the Mrs.

47
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,270
in-game.

48
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:57,117
She used to live in the U .S.,
and we fell for each other hard.

49
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:00,217
A year later, she was here,
running the place with me.

50
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:03,640
Y 'all never know what life's
got planned for you. Aww.

51
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:07,700
If Klein heard that story,
he'd pop a blood vessel.

52
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,433
Anyway, we got married.

53
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:13,097
Next big step was getting
ourselves a pair of NerveGear rigs.

54
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:16,239
But when the time came, we
could only pre-order one.

55
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:20,177
I remember we played some game
to see who'd get to try it first.

56
00:04:20,260 --> 00:04:23,495
I'm glad it was me who cracked
the seal on it, not her.

57
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:24,896
Still feel that way.

58
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,497
The assault team was the only ticket out.

59
00:04:28,580 --> 00:04:30,521
That's why I joined up with them.

60
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:34,072
All I wanted was to get back
to this place and to my lady.

61
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,400
I know what you mean.

62
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,020
I wanted to get back to my family, too.

63
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,301
It's what kept me alive in there.

64
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,477
You and the assault team, brother.

65
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:44,390
Hell, man.

66
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:48,835
I bet every player in Ironcrat felt
the same way about going home again.

67
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,240
Right, Asuna?

68
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,305
Ain't that what motivated you?

69
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,620
No, not really.

70
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:57,001
I mean, it's complicated
between me and my family.

71
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,257
I guess that's why there
were a couple times in

72
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:03,046
there I almost forgot
what I was fighting for.

73
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:06,677
Sometimes I felt like I
didn't belong anywhere.

74
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,120
Real and virtual were both dead ends.

75
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:12,357
But then, I met Kirito.

76
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,911
He gave me something I could come home to.

77
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,357
A place that felt more like a home.

78
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:20,140
Than anything I ever
had in the real world.

79
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,497
I was happy.

80
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:25,117
Even though I knew once SAO was cleared.

81
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,612
Our cabin would be gone.

82
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:29,737
But I knew deep down
that one day, somehow.

83
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:32,300
I'd have a home again with Kirito and Yui.

84
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:35,197
That's what finally gave
me the strength to fight.

85
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:36,339
And keep fighting.

86
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:38,240
It gave me hope?

87
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:49,505
Speaking of Ironcrad kiddies, the mod's
just posted some info on the next update.

88
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:51,900
It's mostly typical stuff.

89
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:55,017
They're going to be adding
new weapons and sword skills,

90
00:05:55,100 --> 00:06:00,260
but they're also going to be unlocking
floors 21 to 30 in new Ironcrad. Boom.

91
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,217
Wait, do you know what that means?

92
00:06:03,300 --> 00:06:09,460
If we beat the boss on Floor 21, we have
a chance to buy that log cabin again.

93
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:15,160
Yeah, yeah, but there's been a ton of
little changes to New Aincrad lately.

94
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:19,217
It sucked to get our hopes up just
to find our cabin's not there.

95
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:22,520
Yeah, it would, but I know it's there.

96
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:25,720
It'll be waiting for us,
just like how we left it.

97
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:31,417
Well, y 'all better get a move on then.

98
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,740
Update goes live Christmas Eve.

99
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:59,560
Seiya, Sha, Lindo, Ashina,
Bart, Amy, or Sparrow!

100
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:10,450
Naaaaaaahhhh!

101
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:15,290
Aaaaah!

102
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:16,870
Aaaaaah!

103
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,960
Aaaaaah! Aaaah! Ha! Ha! Ha!

104
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,080
I'm goin' in!

105
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,430
Asuna!

106
00:08:09,513 --> 00:08:10,343
Keep going!

107
00:08:10,426 --> 00:08:12,660
I've got your back! Asuna! You and me!

108
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,100
Watch out, Daddy!

109
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,456
It's about to punch!

110
00:08:18,420 --> 00:08:19,250
Watch out!

111
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:36,160
Come, kill me, fall me!

112
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,480
I get ya!

113
00:08:42,580 --> 00:08:43,410
Whoa!

114
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:48,020
All right!

115
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:50,600
We made it to floor 22! What do you do?

116
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:05,097
Hey, Asuna, if you're hanging around
because of the teleport gate, don't bother.

117
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:06,298
We can activate it.

118
00:09:11,060 --> 00:09:12,413
Thanks a lot, you guys!

119
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:43,020
Are you seeing this?

120
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:15,480
Here we go. You ready?

121
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:27,100
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

122
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,440
I'm home.

123
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,157
Oh my god, seriously?

124
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,800
Hey, Asuna, wake up!

125
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,853
That goes for you, too!

126
00:11:27,260 --> 00:11:28,837
God, would you look at that?

127
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:31,220
It's like he's daring us to stay awake.

128
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I'll make some more tea
and it'll wake us right up.

129
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,260
Hey, look!

130
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:41,581
I guess it stopped snowing
while we were sleeping.

131
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:45,000
Oh, have you heard the news? What?

132
00:11:45,420 --> 00:11:46,773
You know, about second.

133
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:48,942
Don't tell me you haven't heard.

134
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:50,830
Zekken?

135
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,150
Zekken?

136
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,868
Is that some kind of
rare item or something?

137
00:11:57,280 --> 00:11:58,110
Er, wrong.

138
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,797
It's the name of a player.

139
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,337
Actually, it's not their handle.

140
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:02,949
It's more like a nickname.

141
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:06,597
Anyway, this player's so badass,
someone called him Zekken.

142
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,777
The name caught on and there you go.

143
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:10,560
It means absolute sword.

144
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:12,677
Ultimate sword's better, though.

145
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,642
Either way, this player's tough.

146
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:15,890
Really?

147
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:22,220
So, uh, when did you first
hear about this second person?

148
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:23,630
I don't know.

149
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:27,397
I guess maybe the first time was
around New Year's or something.

150
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:30,240
Maybe a week or so ago? Oh, duh.

151
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,777
That explains why you're so
out of the loop about it.

152
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:36,566
You've been at your family's
compound in Kyoto this whole time.

153
00:12:36,820 --> 00:12:37,650
Mama.

154
00:12:37,733 --> 00:12:40,237
I was having a good time,
but you had to bring that up.

155
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:43,277
Listen to the rich girl
rebelling against her cushy life.

156
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,237
Sounds like a drag.

157
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:46,117
A drag is exactly what it was.

158
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,788
I had to sit on my knees in a
kimono all day greeting people.

159
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:52,240
I brought my atmosphere along,

160
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:55,197
thinking I could dive at night
while everyone was asleep.

161
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,339
But you know what?

162
00:12:56,940 --> 00:13:00,300
The guest house I was in
didn't have Wi-Fi. Fun, right?

163
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,460
It wasn't.

164
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,597
Asuna? Asuna?

165
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:38,900
You even listening? Hello?

166
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,800
Huh? Sorry.

167
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:43,057
I just remembered something lame.

168
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,757
I wonder what that could be.

169
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,977
Were your folks trying to
hook you up with someone?

170
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,040
No, not at all.

171
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:49,573
Forget I said anything.

172
00:13:50,660 --> 00:13:52,160
Okay, okay, just kidding.

173
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:56,713
So, anyway, is this tough new
player a PKer or something?

174
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,057
Mama, just a duelist, that's all.

175
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,846
Were they in any tournaments?

176
00:14:01,440 --> 00:14:02,270
Nope.

177
00:14:02,353 --> 00:14:04,177
As far as I know, this
player's a total noob.

178
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:07,797
I have a feeling they might have
converted over from another game, though.

179
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,197
You should see their skill stats.

180
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:10,751
They're through the roof.

181
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:13,040
You know how on floor 24,

182
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,897
there's that tiny little island
just north of the main town?

183
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,568
The one with the huge tree?

184
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,880
Well, every day at 3 o 'clock,

185
00:14:20,120 --> 00:14:25,120
you know who shows up under that tree,
waiting to take on any challenger one-on-one.

186
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:31,597
Zeken started by posting
this opponent's wanted

187
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:34,151
notice on the MMO Tomorrow bulletin board.

188
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,580
Folks wanted to teach this
cocky all noob lesson,

189
00:14:37,780 --> 00:14:40,557
so on the first day, about
30 players showed up.

190
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:42,717
It didn't go so well for him though.

191
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:46,817
But they lost all of
them one after the other.

192
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:51,917
And get this, none of them managed to chip
off more than 30 percent of seconds hp.

193
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,480
That's a badass.

194
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:56,757
I can't believe how good second is.

195
00:14:56,840 --> 00:15:00,320
Who thought a newbie to the
game could fly as good as bad?

196
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:03,777
It took me at least six
months to learn how to fly

197
00:15:03,860 --> 00:15:06,801
and fight at the same time
and I'm still learning.

198
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,450
stuff.

199
00:15:11,533 --> 00:15:12,363
I, I did it.

200
00:15:12,446 --> 00:15:15,037
Did you fight Zekken too? Not even.

201
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,020
I'm no dummy.

202
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,104
I watched one duel and I knew I

203
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,190
didn't stand a chance.

204
00:15:19,273 --> 00:15:22,537
If you want to know what it was like,
why don't you ask Liz and Leafa?

205
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:24,257
They took Zekken on yesterday.

206
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,197
They fought and lost
like a couple of champs.

207
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:27,633
Please don't remind me.

208
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:33,577
Good learning experience though.

209
00:15:33,660 --> 00:15:34,537
It's snowing.

210
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:36,080
Yeah, pretty isn't it?

211
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,800
So anyway, back to Zek 'in.

212
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,437
If this player is as strong as you say,

213
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:47,337
it's only a matter of time before
there are no more challengers to face.

214
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:48,597
I don't know about that.

215
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:51,937
There's a pretty cool prize
on the line, don't you know?

216
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:52,850
Really?

217
00:15:52,933 --> 00:15:53,763
What is it?

218
00:15:53,846 --> 00:15:55,357
Some kind of rare item or something?

219
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,146
Nope, it's nothing like that.

220
00:15:57,300 --> 00:16:00,477
Whoever beats Zek 'in will
get an original sword skill.

221
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:03,795
It's a special move that's
supposed to be super strong.

222
00:16:04,140 --> 00:16:05,820
An original sword skill?

223
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,130
Hmm.

224
00:16:08,213 --> 00:16:09,043
What type?

225
00:16:09,126 --> 00:16:09,956
How many hits?

226
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:12,230
Hmm.

227
00:16:12,313 --> 00:16:14,861
Well, it's a general skill
for a one-handed sword.

228
00:16:15,220 --> 00:16:16,637
Oh, but here's the thing.

229
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,100
It's an Head combo!

230
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,460
No way, 11?

231
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:23,517
The strongest original sword
skill being used right now.

232
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,188
How many hits does it have?

233
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:28,937
That'd be the one General Eugene
developed, the Volcanic Blazer.

234
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:31,079
It's supposed to be an Head combo.

235
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:35,200
He hasn't passed it on to anyone
else yet, and I doubt he ever will.

236
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:39,851
I guess that explains why so many players
keep lining up to challenge Zekken.

237
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:42,717
Have any of you seen this
sword skill in action?

238
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:43,630
Mama.

239
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:47,337
I heard Zekken demoed it on the
first day of the duels, though.

240
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:49,773
Apparently it blew mines left and right.

241
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:53,993
But since then, it hasn't been
used in any of the fights.

242
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:56,717
Maybe the reason for
that's because there hasn't

243
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,597
been anyone tough enough
to get Zekken to use it.

244
00:16:59,680 --> 00:17:01,700
Whoever does has my respect.

245
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,300
Leafa, what happened
when you fought Zekken?

246
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,080
Besides losing?

247
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:13,180
It was going good till our
HP's dropped below 60%, but...

248
00:17:15,480 --> 00:17:19,340
In the end, Zekken beat me,
using nothing but default skills.

249
00:17:20,180 --> 00:17:21,010
Really?

250
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:24,509
Oh, I can't believe I
almost forgot to ask.

251
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:27,700
What's Zekin's race and
weapon of choice? An imp.

252
00:17:27,960 --> 00:17:29,837
The main weapon's a one-handed sword.

253
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:33,760
It's about as skinny as your
rapier, Asuna, but only just.

254
00:17:34,460 --> 00:17:36,420
And Zekin's super fast, too.

255
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:39,357
I couldn't even see the
attacks coming at me.

256
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:41,317
That's never happened to me before.

257
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,812
I'm still kinda shocked.

258
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:44,680
A speed type, huh?

259
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:49,140
If you had a hard time tracking
Zekken, I doubt I'd be able to either.

260
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:52,361
I know someone who might, though.

261
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:53,510
Mr.

262
00:17:53,593 --> 00:17:55,097
Sleepyhead's the fastest player I've seen.

263
00:17:55,180 --> 00:17:56,533
What do you guys think?

264
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:59,309
Would Kirito go for
that kind of challenge?

265
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:02,470
What?

266
00:18:02,553 --> 00:18:03,383
What'd I say?

267
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:05,230
Nothing.

268
00:18:05,313 --> 00:18:06,957
It's just Kazutou already tried it.

269
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:09,400
And boy, did he lose spectacularly.

270
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,200
I don't believe it.

271
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:14,516
Was he holding back?

272
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,070
Hmm.

273
00:18:17,153 --> 00:18:18,288
Kind of hard for me to say.

274
00:18:18,420 --> 00:18:20,457
From where I was standing,
it looked like it.

275
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,370
Yeah,

276
00:18:21,453 --> 00:18:25,037
but then I don't think I'm really the best
person to judge whether he was or wasn't.

277
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:28,414
He didn't use that dual-wielding
trick, that's for sure.

278
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:31,360
So I guess in a way, he
wasn't going all out.

279
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:33,759
But you know what?

280
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:36,011
That kind of makes sense.

281
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:38,840
I mean, it's a duel in a normal game.

282
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:43,933
There's no reason for Kitty to fight
like his life depended on it anymore.

283
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:48,885
The only time he'll take a fight seriously
now is if the game stops being a game.

284
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:51,886
When the virtual world
becomes the real world.

285
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:56,497
In a way, I hope he never goes
full tilt in a battle ever again.

286
00:18:56,580 --> 00:18:58,698
and he's kind of had enough of that.

287
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:02,647
I mean, heck, he gets into enough
trouble on his own as it is.

288
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:06,928
Yeah, I guess you're right.

289
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:12,277
Well, from where I was standing,
I got a different impression.

290
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:15,184
I think Kazuto was
definitely giving it his all.

291
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,797
He seemed serious and
focused and determined.

292
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,233
He put up a good fight.

293
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,125
At one point, though,
something weird happened.

294
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:26,497
Right before the duel was
over, they were locking swords.

295
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:29,080
And then, they both just stopped.

296
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,937
It looked like Kazuto was
saying something to Zekken.

297
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:35,902
I couldn't hear what
because of all the cheering.

298
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:40,011
And then, all of a sudden, they
backed off from each other.

299
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:45,167
Zekken charged him, but Kazuto couldn't
dodge it, and that's how the duel ended.

300
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,470
Really?

301
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:48,817
What were they talking about?

302
00:19:48,900 --> 00:19:49,940
I wish I knew.

303
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:52,457
I asked him, but Kazuto wouldn't tell me.

304
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:56,217
Whatever it was, it must be pretty
important to keep to himself.

305
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:57,130
Interesting.

306
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:03,422
Alright then, I guess the only way to find
out what he said is to ask Zekken myself.

307
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:06,031
Huh, you think you're up to the challenge?

308
00:20:06,160 --> 00:20:08,597
I'm not doing it because
I think I can win.

309
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:11,856
Something about this Zekken
person intrigues me is all.

310
00:20:11,980 --> 00:20:12,980
I don't know why,

311
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:17,080
but I think this Zekken person's
here for reasons other than dueling.

312
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:19,186
Yep, that's what I think too.

313
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:21,597
But if you want to find
out what it is, get ready,

314
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:24,537
because you're going to have to put
up as good a fight as your boy Kirito,

315
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:25,450
and then some.

316
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,500
Yeah, I know.

317
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:30,384
Will you guys come cheer me on?

318
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,780
You know we will. It'll be awesome.

319
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,757
We wouldn't miss it for anything.

320
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,757
Which character are
you going to duel with?

321
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:39,487
You still have that
Sylph account, don't you?

322
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:41,980
Hmm, I guess I'll use this one.

323
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:43,832
If Zekin's a speed type,

324
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:48,314
it'll probably come down to who can
hold out the longest rather than DPS.

325
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,437
And that's that.

326
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:53,500
So, 3 o 'clock on the island
on Floor 24, right? Mm-hmm.

327
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:58,060
Then if we meet here tomorrow
at 2.30, we can... Oh, no!

328
00:20:58,260 --> 00:20:59,557
It's already 6 o 'clock!

329
00:20:59,640 --> 00:21:00,977
We'll be late for dinner!

330
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:03,877
I guess we might as well call
it a day and log out, too.

331
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:06,431
Rich girls and their problems, am I right?

332
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:10,857
I can't believe he's still asleep!

333
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,697
I know, he didn't even feel a thing!

334
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:14,220
Hey, Liz, what's up?

335
00:21:15,320 --> 00:21:19,379
A little while ago, you said you
thought Zekken converted over to ALO.

336
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:25,340
The way you described the duels got me
thinking, could Zekken be someone from SAO?

337
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:34,951
That's the impression I got after my duel.

338
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:40,520
I wanted a second opinion, so after Kirito
lost his, I asked him what he thought.

339
00:21:41,840 --> 00:21:43,840
So what did Kirito have to say?

340
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:47,137
He said that even though the
skills were through the roof,

341
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:49,437
Zekin's definitely not a player from SAO.

342
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,720
That's not all.

343
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:54,620
Kirito also said that if
Zekken really was from SAO,

344
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:57,801
the dual-wielding skill
wouldn't have gone to him.

345
00:21:57,940 --> 00:21:59,940
It would have gone to Zekken.

346
00:22:22,460 --> 00:22:28,800
I love you, I love you.

347
00:22:49,520 --> 00:22:55,500
I don't know how long you are,
but I don't know how long you are.

348
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:08,660
I'm looking for you to
see you in your eyes.

349
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,980
Next time, Zekken.

350
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:41,640
Thank you.
